267
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:57,889
that haven't been
fully excavated.

268
00:09:57,931 --> 00:09:58,973
Break up with Charlie.

269
00:09:59,015 --> 00:09:59,516
What?

270
00:09:59,558 --> 00:10:01,059
What?

271
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:06,314
Did... did you just say
"break up with Charlie"?

272
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:09,067
Well, yes and no.

273
00:10:09,109 --> 00:10:13,280
Yes, I did say it, and no,
I didn't not say it.

274
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:16,283
Um, kind of inappropriate,
don't you think?

275
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:17,700
Listen... I'm sorry.

276
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:19,578
I just haven't
seen her for so long.

277
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,496
All these feelings
are rushing back.

278
00:10:21,538 --> 00:10:23,998
I'm starting to realize
how much I missed her

279
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,626
and I'm going to need you
to break up with her.

280
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:30,255
Are you serious?

281
00:10:30,297 --> 00:10:32,090
If you say yes,
then I'm serious.

282
00:10:32,132 --> 00:10:33,883
If you say no,
then I'm joking.

283
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:36,010
No.

284
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:37,053
Joking it is.

285
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:42,559
Hi. Sorry I'm late.

286
00:10:42,601 --> 00:10:43,893
Hey. How'd it go with Mike?

287
00:10:43,935 --> 00:10:45,437
Is he going to let
you keep the painting?

288
00:10:45,479 --> 00:10:47,272
No. He really hates it.

289
00:10:47,314 --> 00:10:51,234
But he's going to let me
keep my box of human hair.

290
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:55,155
So, you got
to pick your battles.

291
00:10:55,196 --> 00:10:57,907
But the good news is,
Gladys is yours.

292
00:10:59,117 --> 00:11:02,162
Wow, what's the bad news?

293
00:11:02,203 --> 00:11:03,746
Who's Gladys?

294
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:05,832
Oh, she's that
work of art I made--

295
00:11:05,873 --> 00:11:08,751
you know, with the woman
coming out of the frame.

296
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:13,590
Oh, and Monica
gets to keep her?

297
00:11:13,632 --> 00:11:15,175
In her house?

298
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:16,801
I am so jealous.

299
00:11:18,345 --> 00:11:20,763
Oh, I didn't know
you wanted her, too.

300
00:11:22,516 --> 00:11:25,226
Well, I mean, sure, of course.

301
00:11:25,268 --> 00:11:28,980
But... you already gave
that to Monica, so...

302
00:11:29,022 --> 00:11:31,399
No, no, I would give
her up for you.

303
00:11:31,441 --> 00:11:32,942
No, I couldn't let you do that.

304
00:11:32,984 --> 00:11:34,152
But I want to.

305
00:11:34,194 --> 00:11:35,445
But I don't want you to.

306
00:11:35,487 --> 00:11:37,113
But I insist.

307
00:11:37,155 --> 00:11:39,574
But I insist harder.

308
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:42,327
Okay, girls, girls, stop.

309
00:11:42,369 --> 00:11:43,786
Okay, we'll flip a coin.

310
00:11:43,828 --> 00:11:46,456
Heads she's Rachel's,
tails she's Monica's.

311
00:11:49,334 --> 00:11:51,127
Tails. Monica, she's yours.

312
00:11:51,169 --> 00:11:53,338
That landed in your food.

313
00:11:54,755 --> 00:11:55,798
No, no, that's okay.

314
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,008
You won fair and square.

315
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:58,468
I'm so sad.

316
00:12:00,637 --> 00:12:02,472
Hey, Joe.

317
00:12:02,514 --> 00:12:04,307
What's up?
Bad news.

318
00:12:04,349 --> 00:12:06,601
I watched the tape
and passed it along
to my bosses,

319
00:12:06,643 --> 00:12:08,102
and they weren't
interested.

320
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:09,812
Oh.

321
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:11,814
Sorry, man.

322
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:14,025
Well...

323
00:12:14,067 --> 00:12:15,985
But, uh,
you watched the tape?

324
00:12:16,027 --> 00:12:18,363
Yeah. I-I-I liked it.

325
00:12:18,405 --> 00:12:20,532
But, uh,

326
00:12:20,574 --> 00:12:22,409
my bosses didn't go for it.

327
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:24,661
Stupid sons of bitches!

328
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:31,209
You didn't watch the tape.

329
00:12:31,251 --> 00:12:34,254
What? Of course I did.

330
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:35,922
Look, it's one thing
not to cast me,

331
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,257
but to lie to me?

332
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:39,300
I'm not lying to you--
I watched it.

333
00:12:39,342 --> 00:12:40,510
There, you lied again.

334
00:12:40,552 --> 00:12:41,969
I watched it!

335
00:12:42,011 --> 00:12:43,846
Keep going, Pinocchio!

336
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:46,182
I did!

337
00:12:46,224 --> 00:12:47,934
No, you didn't!
I'm telling you,

338
00:12:47,975 --> 00:12:49,185
I watched the tape!

339
00:12:50,729 --> 00:12:52,397
Did you watch
the tape?

340
00:12:52,439 --> 00:12:53,898
No.

341
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:59,613
So, the selection committee
has chosen the three of you

342
00:12:59,654 --> 00:13:00,947
as our finalists today.

343
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:02,657
The ultimate decision
will be based

344
00:13:02,699 --> 00:13:04,867
upon the answers you give
to the questions I ask here.

345
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:06,411
We're going to start
with Dr. Li.

346
00:13:06,453 --> 00:13:08,996
Dr. Li, you claim the field
is too reliant

347
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:10,789
on the Linnaen taxonomic system.

348
00:13:10,831 --> 00:13:13,710
How do you propose
to correct this problem?
Well, I believe

349
00:13:13,752 --> 00:13:16,212
that the answers lie
in the osteological evidence.

350
00:13:16,254 --> 00:13:17,631
I plan to begin there.

351
00:13:17,672 --> 00:13:18,632
Interesting.

352
00:13:18,673 --> 00:13:21,384
( quietly ):
I guess.

353
00:13:21,426 --> 00:13:24,011
Dr. Biely, your proposal
includes some field work.

354
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:26,139
Where might that take place?
Primarily

355
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:28,516
in the Pierre-Shale
region of South Dakota.

356
00:13:28,558 --> 00:13:29,850
Certainly.
Very well.

357
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:32,937
And, Dr. Geller,
when is my birthday?

358
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:41,154
What? I... I...

359
00:13:42,196 --> 00:13:45,325
Care to venture a guess?

360
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:48,911
May 12?

361
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:51,872
That's not even kind ofclose.

362
00:13:51,914 --> 00:13:53,708
Dr. Li,
how many graduate students

363
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:55,042
will you be needing?

364
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:57,295
Half a dozen.
I see. And Dr. Biely?

365
00:13:57,337 --> 00:14:00,423
Three for excavation
and two for analysis.
Certainly.

366
00:14:00,465 --> 00:14:03,926
Dr. Geller,
which 1965 Shirelles hit

367
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:07,305
was later covered by
a popular British Invasion band?

368
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:13,520
Wha...? I need six
graduate students.

369
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:17,148
No, I'm sorry, we were looking
for "Baby, It's You."

370
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:19,025
"Baby, It's You."

371
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:22,821
Wha... Wait, wait,
wait just a minute.

372
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:26,324
None of my questions
have anything to do
with paleontology.

373
00:14:26,366 --> 00:14:27,492
You're right. I apologize.

374
00:14:27,534 --> 00:14:28,743
Scratch the last question.

375
00:14:28,785 --> 00:14:31,329
Spell "Boscodictiasaur."

376
00:14:32,747 --> 00:14:36,959
Um... I've never heard
of a Bosco... dictiasaur.

377
00:14:37,001 --> 00:14:38,378
Yeah, I just made it up.
Spell it.

378
00:14:42,382 --> 00:14:44,342
Okay. B-O...

379
00:14:44,384 --> 00:14:45,760
No, it starts with a silent "M."

380
00:14:45,802 --> 00:14:48,179
Oh, come on!

381
00:14:54,935 --> 00:14:57,021
I can't believe Joey.

382
00:14:57,063 --> 00:14:58,939
I hate being called a liar.

383
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:00,525
But you are a liar.

384
00:15:01,568 --> 00:15:03,862
What did I just say?

385
00:15:04,863 --> 00:15:06,656
You still here?
Yes,

386
00:15:06,698 --> 00:15:08,825
and I have to say,
I am not just hurt,
I am insulted.

387
00:15:08,867 --> 00:15:11,619
When I tell somebody
I did something...
Okay, hold on,

388
00:15:11,661 --> 00:15:13,329
let me just stop you
right there, okay?

389
00:15:13,371 --> 00:15:14,955
First you lied, right?

390
00:15:14,997 --> 00:15:17,792
Then you lied about lying, okay?

391
00:15:17,834 --> 00:15:20,837
Then you lied about lying
about lying, okay?

392
00:15:20,879 --> 00:15:23,297
So before you lie
about lying about lying

393
00:15:23,339 --> 00:15:26,342
about lying about...
lying about...

394
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:30,346
Stop lying!

395
00:15:30,388 --> 00:15:33,140
Why are you so sure
I didn't watch this tape?

396
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:35,810
You know what?
You want to know why?

397
00:15:35,852 --> 00:15:36,853
Well, this is going well.

398
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:41,023
Here's how I know
you didn't watch the tape, okay?

399
00:15:41,065 --> 00:15:42,817
If you had seen
what was on this tape,

400
00:15:42,859 --> 00:15:45,445
believe me,
you would have some comments.

401
00:15:45,486 --> 00:15:46,780
All right, now,

402
00:15:46,821 --> 00:15:48,989
remember, I got paid
a lot of money for this,

403
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:51,033
and it only aired in Japan.

404
00:15:52,118 --> 00:15:53,994
Icheban.

405
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:57,540
Icheban. Lipstick for men.

406
00:16:10,261 --> 00:16:13,264
Icheban. Lipstick for men.

407
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:14,223
Seiko.

408
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:19,479
And that's how I know
you didn't watch the tape!

409
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,481
( door slams )

410
00:16:21,522 --> 00:16:24,901
He really is a chameleon.

411
00:16:31,407 --> 00:16:36,078
Well, Gladys,
say hello to your new home.

412
00:16:38,957 --> 00:16:40,667
Oh, my.

413
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:42,669
Wow. Oh.

414
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:46,756
She's so nice and big.

415
00:16:46,798 --> 00:16:53,346
Oh, Monica, where are
you going to display
Gladys, oh, so proudly?

416
00:16:53,387 --> 00:16:56,766
Haven't really settled
on a spot yet.

417
00:16:56,808 --> 00:16:58,810
Oh, hey, how about
right above the TV?

418
00:16:58,852 --> 00:17:01,521
That way, it will be
the first thing that you see

419
00:17:01,562 --> 00:17:03,272
when you walk in the door.

420
00:17:03,314 --> 00:17:05,900
Yeah! Yeah!

421
00:17:05,942 --> 00:17:07,944
And you can get rid
of that French poster.

422
00:17:07,986 --> 00:17:10,070
I like that poster.
Really?

423
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:12,699
It doesn't have anything
coming out of it.

424
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,158
Or maybe

425
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,202
there's someplace for her
in your bedroom.

426
00:17:16,243 --> 00:17:17,745
Oh! There's nothing
above your bed!

427
00:17:17,787 --> 00:17:19,121
Are you still here?!

428
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:24,502
Oh, hi.

429
00:17:24,544 --> 00:17:26,713
Hello. Uh,
have you come to ask me

430
00:17:26,754 --> 00:17:29,423
some more paleontology-related
questions?

431
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:32,426
Um, your grandmother's nickname,
perhaps?

432
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:34,220
Ann-Margaret's pant size?

433
00:17:36,347 --> 00:17:38,349
I've come here to apologize.

434
00:17:38,391 --> 00:17:41,686
I think I may have let
my feelings for Charlie

435
00:17:41,728 --> 00:17:44,104
interfere with
the interview process.

436
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:46,357
No. Stop.

437
00:17:46,399 --> 00:17:49,986
Anyway, I decided to
offer you the grant.

438
00:17:51,404 --> 00:17:52,864
Really?

439
00:17:52,906 --> 00:17:56,200
Well, there is just
one small stipulation.

440
00:17:56,242 --> 00:17:58,160
I have to break up with Charlie?

441
00:17:58,202 --> 00:17:59,495
Hey, you got one right.

442
00:18:01,539 --> 00:18:03,249
You're crazy.

443
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:06,460
Crazy or romantic?

444
00:18:06,502 --> 00:18:08,295
Crazy.

445
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:11,465
Or...?

446
00:18:11,507 --> 00:18:12,508
Get out!

447
00:18:19,265 --> 00:18:20,516
Oh, my God!

448
00:18:20,558 --> 00:18:22,435
( gasps )

449
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:24,102
What-what?
Joey,

450
00:18:24,144 --> 00:18:26,814
what is this thing doing here?

451
00:18:26,856 --> 00:18:28,232
I got it from Monica.

452
00:18:28,274 --> 00:18:31,986
She sold it to me for
a very reasonable price.

453
00:18:32,028 --> 00:18:33,905
Joey, we're not keeping this.

454
00:18:33,947 --> 00:18:35,782
But it's an original Buffay.

455
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:41,203
All right, fine,
you can keep it.

456
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:42,830
As long as you don't mind

457
00:18:42,872 --> 00:18:44,206
that she's haunted.

458
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:45,917
Wha-What? Whoa, what? What?

459
00:18:45,959 --> 00:18:47,919
Well, legend has it, Joey,

460
00:18:47,961 --> 00:18:50,880
that she comes alive
when you're asleep.

461
00:18:51,881 --> 00:18:53,633
She climbs

462
00:18:53,674 --> 00:18:56,176
out of the frame

463
00:18:56,218 --> 00:19:00,056
and then drags her half a body
across the floor

464
00:19:00,098 --> 00:19:02,642
just looking for legs to steal.

465
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:04,644
And then

466
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:06,312
with her one good hand,

467
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:10,524
she slowly reaches up

468
00:19:10,566 --> 00:19:12,986
and turns your doorknob...

469
00:19:13,027 --> 00:19:16,155
Get that legless witch
out of here!

470
00:19:21,869 --> 00:19:24,413
Hey, I sold that to Joey.
Yeah?

471
00:19:24,455 --> 00:19:25,832
Well, I told him
it's haunted.

472
00:19:25,873 --> 00:19:27,541
Two can play at this game.
No, too late.

473
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:29,293
You can't give it back.
Yes, I can.

474
00:19:29,335 --> 00:19:31,671
No, you can't--
she's yours!
She's yours!

475
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:33,297
She's yours!
She's yours!

476
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:35,091
Hey.

477
00:19:36,425 --> 00:19:38,302
She's mine!
She's mine!

478
00:19:38,344 --> 00:19:40,178
She's mine!
She's mine!

479
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:42,932
You guys, you guys, you don't
have to fight over her anymore.

480
00:19:42,974 --> 00:19:46,102
Whoever doesn't get Gladys
gets Glynnis.

481
00:19:48,855 --> 00:19:50,230
( gasps )

482
00:19:54,152 --> 00:19:56,112
I want Gladys!

483
00:19:56,154 --> 00:19:57,279
She's mine!
She's mine!

484
00:19:57,321 --> 00:19:58,364
She's mine!

485
00:20:02,118 --> 00:20:04,411
Look, I'm sorry

486
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:05,955
I didn't give them your tape,

487
00:20:05,997 --> 00:20:07,748
and I promise next time
to submit you

488
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:10,208
whether I think you're right
for the part or not.

489
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:12,170
That's not the point, Chandler.

490
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:14,380
The point is that you lied.
I know.

491
00:20:14,421 --> 00:20:15,756
You're right.

492
00:20:15,798 --> 00:20:18,134
What's it going to take
for you to forgive me?

493
00:20:18,176 --> 00:20:19,385
Oh, my God.

494
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:25,725
Excellent.

495
00:20:25,766 --> 00:20:29,020
Now, what do you say?

496
00:20:29,062 --> 00:20:31,313
Lying is wrong.

497
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,940
And?

498
00:20:32,982 --> 00:20:34,150
And?

499
00:20:35,151 --> 00:20:37,653
I'm a pretty little girl.

500
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:41,782
I knew it.

501
00:20:48,789 --> 00:20:53,211
Your ex-boyfriend is insane.

502
00:20:53,252 --> 00:20:54,795
Did you get the grant?
No, I didn't,

503
00:20:54,837 --> 00:20:56,463
and you want to know why?

504
00:20:56,505 --> 00:20:58,758
Because your ex-boyfriend
is still in love with you.

505
00:20:58,799 --> 00:21:00,593
What?
Yeah.

506
00:21:00,634 --> 00:21:01,802
He wouldn't
give me the grant

507
00:21:01,844 --> 00:21:03,137
because I wouldn't
give you up.

508
00:21:03,179 --> 00:21:04,847
Benji isn't in love with me.

509
00:21:04,889 --> 00:21:06,640
I mean, he broke up with me.

510
00:21:06,682 --> 00:21:08,809
And besides,
he's a very ethical man.

511
00:21:08,851 --> 00:21:11,645
Really?

512
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:14,523
Is it ethical to
ask someone in
a grant review,

513
00:21:14,565 --> 00:21:16,609
who was the voice
of Underdog?

514
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:18,277
I'm sure he was
just joking, Ross.

515
00:21:18,318 --> 00:21:19,570
If you don't
believe me,

516
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:21,363
let's go talk
to him, okay?

517
00:21:21,405 --> 00:21:22,823
I'm telling you,
he didn't ask me

518
00:21:22,865 --> 00:21:24,617
onepaleontological
question.

519
00:21:24,658 --> 00:21:25,952
Seriously?
No, oh, I'm sorry,

520
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:27,912
no, he did ask me one.

521
00:21:27,954 --> 00:21:30,206
Uh, how do you spell
"Boscodictiasaur"?

522
00:21:30,248 --> 00:21:32,499
Well, if it's like
the Lake Bosco in Congo,

523
00:21:32,541 --> 00:21:33,918
then M-B-O...

524
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,253
Damn it!

525
00:21:38,714 --> 00:21:40,258
Dr. Geller?

526
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:42,135
Charlie. What are you...
what are you doing here?

527
00:21:42,176 --> 00:21:43,928
I want you to tell
her everything--

528
00:21:43,970 --> 00:21:46,055
about the deal you
tried to make with me,

529
00:21:46,097 --> 00:21:48,015
about the-the crazy
questions you...

530
00:21:48,057 --> 00:21:50,350
Wally Cox.

531
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:53,520
That's the voice of Underdog.

532
00:21:53,562 --> 00:21:56,190
Like I tried to tell you
in the interview, Ross,

533
00:21:56,232 --> 00:21:58,484
this grant is not based
on your knowledge

534
00:21:58,525 --> 00:22:01,361
of pretty useless trivia.
No, no, no,
don't do that.

535
00:22:01,403 --> 00:22:05,699
I want you to look her in
the eyes and tell her the truth.

536
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:07,994
Benji?

537
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:10,454
All right, it's true.

538
00:22:10,496 --> 00:22:13,707
I behaved horribly, but it's
only because I still love you,

539
00:22:13,749 --> 00:22:17,128
and I would do anything
to have you back in my life.

540
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:19,964
Too little too
late, Benji!

541
00:22:20,006 --> 00:22:23,050
I can't believe this.

542
00:22:23,092 --> 00:22:25,052
I never should have
broken up with you.

543
00:22:25,094 --> 00:22:26,720
I think about you all the time.

544
00:22:26,762 --> 00:22:28,055
I mean,

545
00:22:28,097 --> 00:22:30,390
do you ever still
think about me?

546
00:22:30,432 --> 00:22:32,852
No.

547
00:22:32,893 --> 00:22:35,229
Yes.
What?

548
00:22:35,271 --> 00:22:37,690
I don't know
what to say, Benji.

549
00:22:37,731 --> 00:22:42,569
This is all so... romantic.

550
00:22:42,611 --> 00:22:44,404
Or...?

551
00:22:46,907 --> 00:22:49,243
Listen, I know I may be
way out of bounds here,

552
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:52,872
but is there any chance
you would take me back?

553
00:22:55,124 --> 00:22:57,210
Maybe.

554
00:22:57,251 --> 00:22:59,086
Sweetie, this
conversation's

555
00:22:59,128 --> 00:23:01,630
starting to make me
a little uncomfortable.

556
00:23:03,090 --> 00:23:04,717
Oh, God.

557
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:06,927
I am so sorry.

558
00:23:06,969 --> 00:23:08,386
I mean...

559
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:11,891
there's so much history
between us, you know?

560
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:14,643
I'm sorry, too.

561
00:23:22,318 --> 00:23:23,986
I-I love you.

562
00:23:24,028 --> 00:23:25,529
I love you, too.

563
00:23:28,241 --> 00:23:31,493
Okay, that's it--
we are seeing other people!

564
00:23:41,545 --> 00:23:46,342
( fabric ripping slowly )

565
00:23:47,385 --> 00:23:49,387
( ripping continues )

566
00:23:50,054 --> 00:23:51,931
Gladys?

567
00:23:53,182 --> 00:23:55,059
( screaming )

568
00:23:57,061 --> 00:23:59,605
Ha-ha!

569
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:00,898
Third time this week.

570
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,733
Man, this does not get old.

571
00:24:02,775 --> 00:24:05,278
( panting ):
You're mean!

572
00:24:05,319 --> 00:24:08,030
Aw, don't be such a baby.
Please.

573
00:24:08,072 --> 00:24:09,073
( screams )

574
00:24:10,657 --> 00:24:12,659
( shouts )

575
00:24:12,701 --> 00:24:21,835
Captioned by
